ffffffffffp+1023\n     long double: 1.18973e+4932 = 0xf.fffffffffffffffp+16380</code></pre> \n</div>\n<h3 id=\"See_also\">See also</h3>\n<table class=\"t-dsc-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/types/numeric_limits/lowest\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>lowest</span></span></a></div><div><span class=\"t-lines\"><span><span class=\"t-cmark\">[static]</span> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx11\">(C++11)</span></span></span></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  returns the lowest finite value of the given type, i.e. the most negative value for signed types, <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">​<span class=\"nu0\">0</span>​</span></code> for unsigned types <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(public static member function)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/types/numeric_limits/min\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>min</span></span></a></div><div><span class=\"t-lines\"><span><span class=\"t-cmark\">[static]</span></span></span></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  returns the smallest finite value of the given non-floating-point type, or the smallest positive normal value of the given floating-point type <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(public static member function)</span> </td></tr>\n</table>","headings":[{"depth":3,"text":"Return value","id":"Return_value"},{"depth":3,"text":"Example","id":"Example"},{"depth":3,"text":"See also","id":"See_also"}],"breadcrumbs":[{"path":"","title":"C++ reference"},{"path":"types","title":"Type support (basic types, RTTI)"},{"path":"types/numeric_limits","title":"std::numeric_limits"}],"children":[],"map":{"label":"std::numeric_limits<T>::max","children":[{"label":"Declarations","note":"2 declarations; revisions: until C++11, since C++11. Returns the maximum finite value representable by the numeric type T."},{"label":"Return value","children":[{"label":"/* non-specialized */","note":"T()"},{"label":"bool","note":"true"},